// (walldown) RIDE IT DOWN THE WALL AND ONTO THE GROUND (WallRideRideDown). "He doesn't really ride it ... he's basically just bonking off
// the wall and then landing on the ground. He almost needs to ride it down and then, like, transition into the ground better" (19 Oct,
// build 241). Every ride of 19-20 Oct ended by "the ground is near" 85-90 cm up (full gravity on the ride's slow vz), the board rolled
// flat 60-90 cm up and fell 0.13-0.15 s to -440 cm/s. Now the ride goes on down the wall and, when the time left in the deck's own
// descent (its vz, its height and the lowest wheel's, to WR_RD_HEND) comes to the TTR of its tilt, a transition runs over a progress
// s 0 -> 1: the roll flat by s = WR_RD_ROLL (in the air), the heading, pitch and pose weight eased with s, the travel and the board
// controller (held absolutely) turned WallRideExitAngle out from the wall; at s = 1 the flat wheels are ~4 cm up and the game lands it.
// The pop-off stays: when the ground comes too fast to ride down (WR_RD_FAST at full gravity), and for every other end
constexpr float WR_RD_HEND = 11.0f;       // cm: the deck's height over the ground where the transition ends (the flat wheels ~7 cm up: the game drops it the rest)
constexpr float WR_RD_ROLL = 0.65f;       // the share of the transition by which the roll is flat (the real deck follows its target ~0.05-0.1 s late: flat before the wheels come down)
constexpr float WR_RD_MIN_IN = 0.15f;     // s: no transition in a ride's first 0.15 s
constexpr float WR_RD_SETTLE_FLAT = 0.12f;   /* (wallentry 249) s after the deck first lies at 90 % of its tilt that its own descent is still not the ride's (WallRideDownSettle) */
constexpr float WR_RD_GRACE = 0.6f;       // s: WallRideTime stretches this far at the most while descending; and the longest transition
constexpr float WR_RD_SRATE = 10.0f;      // the transition's progress rises at most dt x this a pose (0.10 s at the least)
constexpr float WR_RD_FAST = 0.10f;       // s to the ground at full gravity under which there is no time to ride down: the pop-off
constexpr float WR_POP_CRANK = 0.30f;     // s after a crouch (the ollie's crank) during which a stick pushed up is its release, not a pop
constexpr float WR_POP_RD_S = 0.30f;      // the transition's progress after which a stick pushed up is too late for a pop
volatile int g_wrRdCfg = 1; volatile float g_wrPopUpCfg = 250.0f; volatile float g_wrRdSettleCfg = 0.0f;   /* (wallentry 249) WallRideDownSettle (HJN_Wall("down")'s 3rd; 0 from an older Lua: build 248's) */   // WallRideRideDown, WallRidePopUp (HJN_Wall("down")): a ride takes them as it starts
